AMD operates as a fab-lite semiconductor company, relying on foundries like TSMC. While this reduces capital intensity, it introduces dependency risks during supply chain disruptions. AMD’s focus on data center and AI segments positions it in less cyclical end-markets, but its reliance on a few key customers (e.g., cloud providers) creates concentration risk.  

